1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,563
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:31,573
[Lily] <i>Red Dragon is the head</i>
<i>of the biggest prostitution,</i>

6
00:00:31,656 --> 00:00:34,951
<i>smuggling, white slavery,</i>
<i>kidnap-for-ransom,</i>

7
00:00:35,035 --> 00:00:37,662
<i>and terrorist syndicate</i>
<i>in the Philippines.</i>

8
00:00:37,746 --> 00:00:41,708
<i>That's why I can't understand</i>
<i>why she's coming after me.</i>

9
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:44,586
[Helena] <i>I need to utilize all my power</i>

10
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:48,214
<i>to be able to eliminate Emilia's enemies.</i>

11
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:50,175
<i>Prepare for war, Mercedes.</i>

12
00:00:50,258 --> 00:00:54,054
<i>We will spare neither Julio nor Lily Cruz.</i>

13
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:57,098
[Diego] <i>That business is under</i>
<i>Mercedes Palacio's name.</i>

14
00:00:57,182 --> 00:01:00,226
<i>If my hunch is right,</i>
<i>we'll find Red Dragon there.</i>

15
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:03,271
[Lily] <i>I will make sure I find her.</i>

16
00:01:03,354 --> 00:01:04,898
[Natalie] <i>Whether you like it or not,</i>

17
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:11,279
<i>I'm your master and you are</i>
<i>my tempting and hot slave.</i>

18
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,906
<i>And I need to see you now.</i>

19
00:01:13,573 --> 00:01:15,450
[Madonna] <i>You know,</i>
<i>if you're lucky enough,</i>

20
00:01:15,533 --> 00:01:17,994
<i>you'll be one of the few</i>
<i>to see Red Dragon.</i>

21
00:01:18,078 --> 00:01:20,914
<i>And if things work out,</i>
<i>you might get to meet her.</i>

22
00:01:20,997 --> 00:01:22,957
[Helena] <i>Mercedes, keep an eye on Apollo.</i>

23
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,626
<i>Make sure that he does what's necessary</i>

24
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:27,921
<i>to improve the security detail</i>
<i>and income of this club.</i>

25
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:28,922
<i>Understood, madam.</i>

26
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:31,925
[henchwoman 1] <i>Is she the woman</i>
<i>Boss Apollo requested?</i>

27
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:33,426
[henchwoman 2] <i>What are you doing here?</i>

28
00:01:33,510 --> 00:01:35,011
<i>You're not allowed here.</i>

29
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:38,264
<i>But I think it would be better</i>
<i>if I saw you without a mask.</i>

30
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:45,230
Take him!

31
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:48,900
[suspenseful music playing]

32
00:02:01,287 --> 00:02:02,831
[guns clatter]

33
00:02:04,749 --> 00:02:07,168
[suspenseful music playing]

34
00:02:20,265 --> 00:02:22,559
[henchwomen and Diego grunting]

35
00:02:30,108 --> 00:02:31,442
[grunting continues]

36
00:02:37,282 --> 00:02:39,951
[suspenseful music playing]

37
00:02:43,705 --> 00:02:44,747
[henchwoman 1] Boss!

38
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:48,459
Boss! There's trouble outside!

39
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,671
[Apollo] What?

40
00:02:57,051 --> 00:03:00,221
[suspenseful music playing]

41
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:03,391
[henchwoman grunting]

42
00:03:12,734 --> 00:03:13,610
[Lily] Diego?

43
00:03:16,279 --> 00:03:17,196
Diego.

44
00:03:17,572 --> 00:03:18,990
-What now?
-Let's go.

45
00:03:19,073 --> 00:03:22,118
Red Dragon already left.
Let's get out of here.

46
00:03:22,869 --> 00:03:26,080
[suspenseful music swells, stops]

47
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:28,666
Thank goodness nothing bad
happened to you.

48
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:30,835
Yes, Mom. Diego and I were careful.

49
00:03:30,919 --> 00:03:32,795
We're safe and that's what matters.

50
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:36,466
It's just too bad that
we didn't see Red Dragon.

51
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:37,800
Lily!

52
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,345
You shouldn't have done that.

53
00:03:40,803 --> 00:03:43,223
Do not go after Red Dragon on a whim!

54
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:45,850
I needed to do it, Uncle Damian.

55
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:49,145
I need to know who Red Dragon is

56
00:03:49,229 --> 00:03:50,772
because she's been going after us.

57
00:03:50,855 --> 00:03:52,523
If I don't make a move,

58
00:03:52,607 --> 00:03:54,776
then all of us will be in danger.

59
00:03:56,361 --> 00:03:58,529
What's important, Mom,
is that Diego and I are safe.

60
00:03:58,863 --> 00:04:02,242
I know, Lily, but your uncle is right.

61
00:04:02,325 --> 00:04:03,743
Don't go back there.

62
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,995
[tense music playing]

63
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:10,208
Even if I shouldn't, I have to.

64
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:13,962
The girls Red Dragon prostitutes
are minors.

65
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,298
I have to help those girls.

66
00:04:18,675 --> 00:04:21,177
[tense music playing]

67
00:04:31,104 --> 00:04:33,773
["La Vie En Rose" instrumental playing]

68
00:04:35,775 --> 00:04:37,485
[birds chirping]

69
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,490
[young Julio] <i>Flowers for you.</i>

70
00:04:42,865 --> 00:04:44,033
[young Helena] <i>Thank you.</i>

71
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,870
[young Julio]
<i>I have something else for you.</i>

72
00:04:49,038 --> 00:04:50,415
<i>It's a promise ring.</i>

73
00:04:52,292 --> 00:04:53,209
<i>Helena, I love you.</i>

74
00:04:54,961 --> 00:04:58,339
<i>I promise to marry you</i>
<i>and be with you forever.</i>

75
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:12,312
["La Vie En Rose" instrumental playing]

76
00:05:29,203 --> 00:05:31,497
No woman has ever toyed

77
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:37,420
with Julio Ardiente and not regretted it.

78
00:05:37,503 --> 00:05:40,548
["La Vie En Rose" instrumental playing]

79
00:05:49,223 --> 00:05:50,850
[objects clatter]

80
00:05:57,565 --> 00:05:59,358
-[Madonna] Hi, sir!
-[upbeat electronic music plays]

81
00:05:59,442 --> 00:06:01,152
-[Madonna] How was--I'm good!
-[man] How are you?

82
00:06:04,447 --> 00:06:05,448
This is the police!

83
00:06:05,531 --> 00:06:07,325
-Nobody move!
-[people shouting indistinctly]

84
00:06:07,408 --> 00:06:09,660
[Madonna] Hey! Hey!
We're just working here!

85
00:06:09,744 --> 00:06:11,996
[officer] Ma'am, ma'am,
sit down. Sit down.

86
00:06:12,080 --> 00:06:13,289
[suspenseful music playing]

87
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:14,373
What's the meaning of this?

88
00:06:14,457 --> 00:06:16,209
-It's a raid, sir.
-You got a warrant?

89
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:17,835
Yes, we do. Now, come with us.

90
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:20,630
[officer] Boys, take 'em away!

91
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,882
[suspenseful music playing]

92
00:06:25,051 --> 00:06:27,553
[officer] Take them! Move! Move!

93
00:06:29,055 --> 00:06:30,014
Go!

94
00:06:30,890 --> 00:06:33,184
[indistinct shouting]

95
00:06:33,267 --> 00:06:36,104
[suspenseful music playing]

96
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,410
[both squeal in fear]

97
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:53,329
Move! Move!

98
00:06:53,412 --> 00:06:54,914
This is a raid! Nobody move!

99
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:58,251
-Move! Move! Move! Hurry! Move!
-[women crying, squealing]

100
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,169
-[officer 1] Move!
-[officer 2] Hurry! Go! Go!

101
00:07:00,253 --> 00:07:02,255
-[officer 1] Move! Move!
-[officer 2] Go! Hurry!

102
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:03,923
[officer 3] Hands in the air!
Hands in the air!

103
00:07:04,006 --> 00:07:05,550
-[officer 4] Hands in the air!
-[officer 3] The minors!

104
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:07,343
-[officer 2] The minors!
-[officer 4] Get the minors out!

105
00:07:07,426 --> 00:07:08,886
-Get them!
-Come on, let's go!

106
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:12,640
Come with us. Hurry! Move!

107
00:07:12,723 --> 00:07:14,809
-[officer 2] Move it!
-[officer 4] Hurry! Hurry!

108
00:07:14,892 --> 00:07:17,019
[suspenseful music playing]

109
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:20,982
[women squealing]

110
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,612
[officer] <i>We rescued all the female minors</i>

111
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:27,530
<i>locked in the club.</i>

112
00:07:28,906 --> 00:07:30,199
<i>Thanks for the tip.</i>

113
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:32,535
We were able to save them because of you.

114
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:37,457
Thank you, sir.
Please do everything you can

115
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:40,751
to return those girls
to their respective families.

116
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,964
By the way, were you able
to capture Red Dragon?

117
00:07:45,548 --> 00:07:46,716
There was no sign of her, ma'am.

118
00:07:47,675 --> 00:07:51,512
[suspenseful music intensifies]

119
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:03,858
The police raided Club Dragonfly.

120
00:08:03,941 --> 00:08:06,777
They were able to shut it down,
arrest our staff,

121
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:08,070
and confiscate all our profits.

122
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:09,989
Tell our connections in the police

123
00:08:10,072 --> 00:08:14,243
to make sure your name isn't
linked to the club in any way.

124
00:08:14,702 --> 00:08:15,745
Copy, madam.

125
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,832
By the way, where's Apollo?

126
00:08:20,958 --> 00:08:22,919
Escaped like a coward.

127
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:24,795
That idiot!

128
00:08:25,129 --> 00:08:26,797
That man should be burned to ashes.

129
00:08:27,340 --> 00:08:28,716
[exhales sharply] Mercedes…

130
00:08:30,301 --> 00:08:36,641
Call our best man to hunt down Apollo.

131
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:40,895
What are you still doing there?!

132
00:08:41,562 --> 00:08:42,605
Excuse me.

133
00:08:43,856 --> 00:08:44,899
[exhales slowly]

134
00:08:56,410 --> 00:08:58,079
Finally, Madrigal.

135
00:08:59,038 --> 00:09:00,748
Do you like making me wait?

136
00:09:03,084 --> 00:09:04,335
You're late!

137
00:09:05,419 --> 00:09:06,462
[smooches]

138
00:09:07,046 --> 00:09:08,256
But it's okay.

139
00:09:09,590 --> 00:09:11,592
You made me miss you a little bit.

140
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,219
So, I'll punish you later.

141
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,763
What do you want from me now?

142
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,015
Wow! [laughs]

143
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:21,852
Don't act as if you don't like
our secret arrangement.

144
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,855
I have what you need,

145
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:29,360
and you have exactly what I want.

146
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:32,655
Aren't we the perfect match?

147
00:09:33,364 --> 00:09:34,407
Hmm?

148
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:40,121
[Anna] Jepoy!

149
00:09:41,122 --> 00:09:41,914
You witch!

150
00:09:41,998 --> 00:09:43,749
-Anna!
-Get away from him, you flirt!

151
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:44,959
What are you doing here?!

152
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:47,837
I followed you to stop you
from seeing that woman!

153
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:49,255
Ooh…

154
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:50,423
[laughs]

155
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:53,342
-Go home!
-We have an angry guest.

156
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:57,179
Aren't you that little provincial girl

157
00:09:57,430 --> 00:09:59,181
who's so scheming,

158
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:03,227
and who pretended to be Lily Cruz?

159
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:04,312
[Anna] Tell us the truth!

160
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:05,605
What do you want from my friend?!

161
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:07,648
-You'll just get him in trouble!
-Go home.

162
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:09,108
Go home.

163
00:10:09,525 --> 00:10:14,655
Unless you're Madrigal's
girlfriend, guess what.

164
00:10:14,947 --> 00:10:18,409
It's none of your business.

165
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:19,910
Natalie.

166
00:10:22,246 --> 00:10:26,626
Talk to that little drama princess.

167
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:31,088
Your friend looks very jealous, Madrigal.

168
00:10:32,214 --> 00:10:34,717
I'll leave you two to your drama.

169
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:40,222
[subtle tense music playing]

170
00:10:46,937 --> 00:10:48,147
[car engine starts]

171
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:55,363
Anna. Wait. Anna, let's talk!

172
00:10:55,446 --> 00:10:57,073
There's nothing to talk about, Jepoy.

173
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,824
It's pretty obvious
there's something going on

174
00:10:58,908 --> 00:11:01,952
between you two.
You think I don't know her?

175
00:11:02,453 --> 00:11:05,247
She's a criminal, Jepoy.
She'll get you in trouble!

176
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:07,083
Anna, I'm not doing anything wrong.

177
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:10,961
If that's true, then why did you
keep this from us?

178
00:11:11,712 --> 00:11:13,422
Why hide it, Jepoy?

179
00:11:13,506 --> 00:11:15,674
Because it's hard for me.
Even if I told you,

180
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:17,218
none of you would've believed me.

181
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:22,681
It hurts to admit
that I let Natalie use me.

182
00:11:26,560 --> 00:11:28,312
Aren't we enough, Jepoy?

183
00:11:29,271 --> 00:11:33,484
We're your friends. We trusted you, Jepoy.

184
00:11:33,651 --> 00:11:36,987
Now, how can we trust you when
you're keeping secrets from us?

185
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:40,783
Do we still have your loyalty
or is it now with that woman?!

186
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:46,997
Anna, you are my family. You, Lily.

187
00:11:47,498 --> 00:11:49,625
We're family.
What kind of question is that?

188
00:11:50,626 --> 00:11:52,378
But how can we trust you now?

189
00:11:55,089 --> 00:11:56,424
I'm sorry, Anna.

190
00:11:58,592 --> 00:11:59,677
I'm sorry.

191
00:12:00,845 --> 00:12:02,847
I thought you were my friend, Jepoy.

192
00:12:03,305 --> 00:12:05,891
Friends don't keep secrets
from each other.

193
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:11,480
Anna. Anna, wait. Anna. Anna! Anna!

194
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:14,567
[dramatic music playing]

195
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,948
Why don't you just tell me straight up?

196
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:23,117
You're hiding something from me.

197
00:12:23,576 --> 00:12:24,952
Are you talking to me, Papa?

198
00:12:25,911 --> 00:12:27,705
[chuckling] We're the only ones here.

199
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,374
Please, drop the little act, Emilia.

200
00:12:30,875 --> 00:12:32,960
I don't know what
you're talking about, Papa.

201
00:12:34,503 --> 00:12:35,421
[deep sigh]

202
00:12:35,754 --> 00:12:37,756
I can sense it, Emilia.

203
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:42,761
You can't hide anything from me.
I know you've met your mother.

204
00:12:42,845 --> 00:12:44,221
[subtle tense music playing]

205
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:47,349
Huh? But my mother's dead!

206
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:49,977
Can you stop all this drama?

207
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:53,230
I am not talking about Esmeralda.

208
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,524
I am talking about your real mother!

209
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:56,984
So, it's true, Papa?!

210
00:12:57,485 --> 00:13:00,446
My real mother's still alive?!
Is it true?!

211
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,366
Please, enough with your drama.

212
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:05,534
I've known for a long time

213
00:13:05,618 --> 00:13:09,205
that you are aware that Esmeralda
was not your real mother!

214
00:13:09,622 --> 00:13:12,416
How could you lie to me, Papa?
How could you do this to me?

215
00:13:12,500 --> 00:13:14,460
So, that explains the awful way
you've been treating me.

216
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:15,503
I'm an illegitimate child!

217
00:13:15,586 --> 00:13:18,255
I hate you, Papa! I super hate you!

218
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:20,799
[gloomy music playing]

219
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:29,975
She's been watching too many soap operas.

220
00:13:37,525 --> 00:13:40,486
-[laughing]
-[suspenseful music playing]

221
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:43,989
Now, it's my time to play you, Papa.

222
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:46,450
-[suspenseful music intensifies]
-[chuckling]

223
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:57,920
Camia. Um… I'm sorry.

224
00:13:58,379 --> 00:13:59,338
It's okay, Damian.

225
00:13:59,421 --> 00:14:01,924
No, Camia. It isn't okay.

226
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:05,386
I shouldn't have raised my voice
at Lily the other day.

227
00:14:06,136 --> 00:14:08,222
I'm just worried for her, that's all.

228
00:14:09,265 --> 00:14:11,225
[sighs] I understand, Damian.

229
00:14:11,809 --> 00:14:13,978
But I hope you'll try to know her better.

230
00:14:14,812 --> 00:14:18,148
She takes after your brother.
She's fearless.

231
00:14:19,733 --> 00:14:21,235
But we know what happened to my brother.

232
00:14:21,944 --> 00:14:23,237
They killed him.

233
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:25,531
I don't want that to happen to Lily.

234
00:14:25,614 --> 00:14:27,575
I don't want that to happen either.

235
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:30,411
But, Damian, there's no stopping Lily

236
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:31,412
from fulfilling her mission.

237
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:36,041
And as her mother, the best
I can do is give her advice,

238
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,668
and fight by her side.

239
00:14:38,961 --> 00:14:42,631
I won't let Lily suffer
the same fate Dante did.

240
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:45,634
They'll have to kill me first
before they can kill her.

241
00:14:47,303 --> 00:14:49,305
[cell phone vibrating]

242
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:54,435
I'm sorry, Camia.
I need to get back to work.

243
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,979
Take care of yourselves, okay?

244
00:14:57,062 --> 00:14:59,148
[unsettling piano music playing]

245
00:15:11,493 --> 00:15:13,996
[foreboding music playing]

246
00:15:30,596 --> 00:15:34,475
Jaguar. It's so nice to see you.

247
00:15:35,184 --> 00:15:37,311
[in distorted voice] You called
for me, Madam Red Dragon?

248
00:15:38,854 --> 00:15:40,189
I have a mission for you.

249
00:15:40,272 --> 00:15:42,024
[suspenseful music playing]

250
00:15:43,984 --> 00:15:45,527
Find Apollo.

251
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,871
Are you questioning my order?

252
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,248
It's not like that, Madam Red Dragon.

253
00:15:58,332 --> 00:15:59,416
But you have a lot of men.

254
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:01,835
You don't need my skills
to bring Apollo here.

255
00:16:03,837 --> 00:16:10,302
What if I tell you…
it's your service that I want?

256
00:16:10,844 --> 00:16:13,263
[suspenseful music playing]

257
00:16:13,889 --> 00:16:14,848
[chuckles]

258
00:16:14,932 --> 00:16:19,019
Very good, Jaguar! Very, very good!

259
00:16:19,103 --> 00:16:20,437
[laughing]

260
00:16:26,068 --> 00:16:29,196
[suspenseful music intensifies]

261
00:16:34,702 --> 00:16:35,661
[birds chirping]

262
00:16:36,203 --> 00:16:38,664
[foreboding music playing]

263
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:43,711
[man 1] Let's get Arnaldo!

264
00:16:43,794 --> 00:16:45,379
-[woman 1] Let's get Arnaldo!
-[man 1] Get him!

265
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:49,341
-Get him! Get him!
-There's Arnaldo!

266
00:16:49,591 --> 00:16:50,801
[woman 3] He should be punished!

267
00:16:51,343 --> 00:16:52,761
-[man 1] Get him!
-[woman 3] Punish him!

268
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:53,929
[man 1] Get him!

269
00:16:54,013 --> 00:16:57,391
You'll never be a saint!

270
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:59,810
A leopard can never change its spots!

271
00:16:59,893 --> 00:17:01,854
-[man 2] Punish him!
-[townspeople] Right! Yeah!

272
00:17:01,937 --> 00:17:03,355
Punish the Ardientes!

273
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:05,816
[indistinct shouting]

274
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:09,903
[man 2] Punish the Ardientes!
Punish the Ardientes!

275
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:11,405
[indistinct shouting]

276
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:15,367
-Stop! Wait! Wait! Wait!
-[dramatic tense music playing]

277
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:16,744
Everyone, calm down.

278
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:19,955
Diego, don't you dare
protect that monster!

279
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:23,667
He has to pay for his family's
sins against us!

280
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:26,879
-That's right!
-That's right!

281
00:17:26,962 --> 00:17:28,255
Hold on! Hold on!

282
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,340
Arnaldo's a changed man.

283
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,593
He's no longer the Arnaldo we all knew.

284
00:17:33,218 --> 00:17:34,636
Let's give him a second chance.

285
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:37,056
-Never!
-Don't let him fool you!

286
00:17:37,139 --> 00:17:41,060
We'll be no better than
criminals if we hurt others.

287
00:17:41,143 --> 00:17:42,978
Violence isn't the solution.

288
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:44,938
Don't let your anger control you.

289
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:48,067
Arnaldo will own up to his mistakes

290
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:50,569
the legal way, through due process.

291
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:53,781
You can't tell us
how to feel about that monster!

292
00:17:53,864 --> 00:17:54,823
[man 2] She's right!

293
00:17:55,824 --> 00:18:01,038
We'll have our day, Arnaldo!
Remember that! Let's go!

294
00:18:03,082 --> 00:18:04,917
[woman 5] Why is he protecting him?

295
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:06,460
I don't understand.

296
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:07,669
[townspeople talking indistinctly]

297
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,880
[woman 5] Why are you protecting him?

298
00:18:09,963 --> 00:18:11,006
[man 2] Let's go!

299
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,348
[somber music playing]

300
00:18:26,939 --> 00:18:29,399
Thank you. Thank you for protecting me.

301
00:18:31,485 --> 00:18:32,569
Thank you.

302
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:37,324
Don't thank me just yet.
You may have changed,

303
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:43,247
but you can't run away
from the crimes you committed.

304
00:18:43,664 --> 00:18:44,706
[sniffles]

305
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:45,833
Uh…

306
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:50,129
If what you say about me is true,

307
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:54,133
I'm ready to face the consequences.

308
00:18:54,883 --> 00:18:55,968
I'll face them.

309
00:18:56,885 --> 00:18:57,928
[sniffles]

310
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:00,097
All that I ask of you…

311
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:03,725
[sniffles]

312
00:19:04,351 --> 00:19:07,479
is to believe that anyone
can change. Even me.

313
00:19:10,858 --> 00:19:13,402
-Thank you.
-[dramatic music playing]

314
00:19:13,986 --> 00:19:15,028
[sniffles]

315
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,961
[foreboding music playing]

316
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:35,924
Madam, why-- why did you call for me?

317
00:19:39,887 --> 00:19:41,763
Why were you hiding from me, Apollo?

318
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:44,266
I wasn't hiding from you, madam!

319
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:47,603
I just needed to lie low because
the cops were looking for me.

320
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:51,440
Liar.

321
00:19:52,316 --> 00:19:53,942
You were hiding from me

322
00:19:55,444 --> 00:19:58,071
because cops raided Club Dragonfly.

323
00:19:58,155 --> 00:19:59,865
Thanks to your negligence!

324
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:01,617
[Apollo breathing heavily]

325
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:05,495
Give me another chance, madam.
I'm begging you. I'm sorry.

326
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,664
It won't happen again.
I'll do better next time.

327
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:16,381
Apollo, why don't we let
the gods decide on your fate?

328
00:20:17,299 --> 00:20:20,844
[gloomy music playing]

329
00:20:27,559 --> 00:20:33,398
Heads, you live. Tails, you die.

330
00:20:33,482 --> 00:20:38,195
[suspenseful music playing]

331
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:44,326
What will it be, Apollo?
Are you ready, huh?

332
00:20:49,706 --> 00:20:50,666
[spins coin]

333
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:53,835
[suspenseful music playing]

334
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:07,266
[laughs]

335
00:21:10,727 --> 00:21:14,398
Madam, thank you so much.
I swear, I'll do a better job.

336
00:21:16,942 --> 00:21:18,193
But, wait.

337
00:21:22,030 --> 00:21:23,657
[suspenseful music playing]

338
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,700
Look.

339
00:21:26,159 --> 00:21:27,077
Tails.

340
00:21:33,208 --> 00:21:34,084
You die.

341
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:36,795
[suspenseful music playing]

342
00:21:36,878 --> 00:21:39,339
[breathing heavily]

343
00:21:40,007 --> 00:21:42,175
Madam! Have mercy on me!

344
00:21:44,845 --> 00:21:46,221
Madam! Have mercy…

345
00:21:46,722 --> 00:21:48,015
Have mercy on me!

346
00:21:49,182 --> 00:21:51,601
[suspenseful music playing]

347
00:22:13,623 --> 00:22:15,208
[screaming]

348
00:22:15,292 --> 00:22:16,460
Have mercy on me!

349
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:19,963
[screaming continues]

350
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:24,760
Look at Apollo.

351
00:22:25,761 --> 00:22:28,680
That's what I want to do
to my new enemies.

352
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:33,935
-Because fire melts gold.
-[screaming continues]

353
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:38,065
I want to burn Lily Cruz alive!

354
00:22:38,148 --> 00:22:40,567
[suspenseful music playing]

355
00:22:56,875 --> 00:22:59,669
[ominous music playing]

356
00:23:03,965 --> 00:23:06,760
[Damian] <i>You have no idea</i>
<i>how vicious your enemies are.</i>

357
00:23:07,969 --> 00:23:09,596
<i>But I'm here.</i>

358
00:23:10,138 --> 00:23:12,432
<i>I will protect you from Red Dragon,</i>

359
00:23:14,976 --> 00:23:16,728
<i>even if it kills me.</i>

360
00:23:16,812 --> 00:23:20,107
[tense music playing]

361
00:23:32,202 --> 00:23:33,620
[engine starts]

362
00:23:41,878 --> 00:23:45,006
[pensive music playing]

363
00:23:49,845 --> 00:23:50,762
Mom.

364
00:23:51,638 --> 00:23:52,597
Lily.

365
00:23:52,681 --> 00:23:53,640
Are you okay?

366
00:23:56,059 --> 00:23:57,144
I'm fine, dear.

367
00:23:57,853 --> 00:23:59,604
I'm just thinking about your uncle.

368
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:06,528
Come on, Mom. Get some rest.

369
00:24:08,446 --> 00:24:09,489
All right.

370
00:24:13,410 --> 00:24:15,954
[Mercedes] Can we still trust Jaguar?

371
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:20,000
He might betray us because
our enemies are related to him.

372
00:24:20,959 --> 00:24:22,961
No, I don't trust him at all.

373
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:25,297
Why don't we kill him?

374
00:24:29,467 --> 00:24:32,220
Mercedes, sometimes, you're an idiot.

375
00:24:34,931 --> 00:24:38,435
We still need to use Jaguar
against Lily Cruz.

376
00:24:40,353 --> 00:24:43,440
For now, we'll let him do what he wants.

377
00:24:43,523 --> 00:24:46,776
I'll tame that cat one day.

378
00:24:48,153 --> 00:24:51,907
Oh, by the way, please call Governor Ruiz,

379
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:53,783
and tell him that it's time for me

380
00:24:53,867 --> 00:24:57,704
to meet my allies as well as my enemies.

381
00:24:58,288 --> 00:25:00,540
Right away. Excuse me.

382
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:02,709
[tense music playing]

383
00:25:13,845 --> 00:25:15,096
Governor Ruiz.

384
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,390
Ms. Cruz. Thank you for coming.

385
00:25:17,641 --> 00:25:19,476
Anything for the people of Ardiente.

386
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:21,811
And the people will definitely
benefit from this.

387
00:25:22,187 --> 00:25:23,521
Let me introduce you to someone.

388
00:25:23,605 --> 00:25:26,233
A philanthropist who wants
to help the townspeople.

389
00:25:26,775 --> 00:25:30,028
I personally reached out
to her so she can help you.

390
00:25:30,946 --> 00:25:32,948
She's the most successful
jeweler in the Philippines,

391
00:25:33,031 --> 00:25:34,616
and she's willing to share her fortunes

392
00:25:34,699 --> 00:25:35,867
with the people of Ardiente.

393
00:25:36,493 --> 00:25:39,412
Oh, okay. Who is she?

394
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:46,753
Lily Cruz, meet Helena Montoya,
CEO of Montoya Industries.

395
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:50,090
[suspenseful music playing]

396
00:25:55,011 --> 00:25:57,138
Lily Cruz, it's nice to meet you.

397
00:25:57,722 --> 00:26:01,142
[suspenseful music playing]

398
00:26:06,773 --> 00:26:09,192
<i>Ms. Cruz, we need to set</i>
<i>a meeting with you</i>

399
00:26:09,276 --> 00:26:10,819
<i>and Mrs. Helena Montoya.</i>

400
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:12,445
<i>Who's Helena Montoya?</i>

401
00:26:12,529 --> 00:26:14,656
<i>She's the CEO of Montoya Industries,</i>

402
00:26:14,739 --> 00:26:17,117
<i>and she's interested in investing</i>

403
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:20,870
<i>in our luxury residences project</i>
<i>in the suburbs.</i>

404
00:26:20,954 --> 00:26:22,998
<i>-Remember Helena Montoya?</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

405
00:26:23,081 --> 00:26:26,042
<i>The philanthropist who wants</i>
<i>to invest in our company.</i>

406
00:26:26,126 --> 00:26:28,920
<i>But I want to review her proposal first.</i>

407
00:26:34,092 --> 00:26:36,386
[gloomy music playing]

408
00:26:38,847 --> 00:26:40,348
Helena Montoya.

409
00:26:41,016 --> 00:26:44,269
The same Helena Montoya who
wants to invest in my company.

410
00:26:44,728 --> 00:26:48,023
That's me.
How come I didn't hear from you?

411
00:26:48,398 --> 00:26:49,441
Oh, sorry.

412
00:26:49,774 --> 00:26:52,944
I'm sure you've heard about
what happened to my properties.

413
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:55,697
That's why I'm more careful now.

414
00:26:55,780 --> 00:26:58,450
I'm still studying your proposal.

415
00:26:58,908 --> 00:27:01,995
I'm sorry to hear that, but no pressure.

416
00:27:02,579 --> 00:27:07,542
I know there are more important
things to consider this time,

417
00:27:07,959 --> 00:27:10,754
especially the well-being
of the people of Ardiente.

418
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:14,924
-Please.
-[chuckles]

419
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:18,386
[sinister music playing]

420
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:22,599
I'd like to thank you, Ms. Montoya,

421
00:27:22,682 --> 00:27:25,643
for your willingness to help the people

422
00:27:25,727 --> 00:27:27,854
of Poblacion Ardiente.

423
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:33,318
I was really moved
when Governor Ruiz told me

424
00:27:33,985 --> 00:27:35,737
what the town has been through.

425
00:27:37,614 --> 00:27:40,617
A place with so much promise
that's ravaged

426
00:27:40,700 --> 00:27:43,078
by crime and corruption.

427
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:48,124
I know you want to help Ardiente.

428
00:27:48,500 --> 00:27:49,584
So, let's work together.

429
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:52,962
Oh, yes, please. Yes.

430
00:27:54,047 --> 00:27:56,841
Poblacion Ardiente needs people like you.

431
00:27:57,092 --> 00:28:00,595
It's rare to find people
who truly want to help.

432
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:03,515
So, what are you proposing?

433
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:06,351
I'm going to have a charity event

434
00:28:06,434 --> 00:28:10,980
to kick-start Oplan Restore
Poblacion Ardiente.

435
00:28:11,606 --> 00:28:13,691
And I want you to spread the news.

436
00:28:13,775 --> 00:28:14,692
Just tell everyone.

437
00:28:14,776 --> 00:28:17,737
Your friends, your neighbors,
your relatives.

438
00:28:19,531 --> 00:28:21,157
Let's help each other.

439
00:28:21,991 --> 00:28:26,704
Together, we can help the people
of Ardiente rise from the ashes.

440
00:28:32,710 --> 00:28:34,462
[tense music playing]

441
00:28:37,674 --> 00:28:40,885
I've read through
all of Helena Montoya's files.

442
00:28:41,720 --> 00:28:43,638
I didn't find any dirt on her.

443
00:28:44,139 --> 00:28:46,391
She has also helped other provinces too.

444
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:51,229
Mom, I still don't trust her.

445
00:28:54,691 --> 00:28:56,985
Do you think you can fool Lily Cruz?

446
00:28:58,778 --> 00:29:02,949
Why, yes. Of course.
But it's not going to be easy.

447
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:06,578
The Ardientes have hardened her heart.

448
00:29:06,661 --> 00:29:08,329
It'll be harder to pierce.

449
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:13,752
But if there's anyone
who could crush Lily Cruz,

450
00:29:14,085 --> 00:29:15,128
that's me.

451
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:19,466
I know exactly what she's doing.

452
00:29:20,300 --> 00:29:22,177
[suspenseful music playing]

453
00:29:22,969 --> 00:29:25,346
Ms. Prianka told me about people like her.

454
00:29:26,097 --> 00:29:31,770
Demons dressed as angels
have the darkest souls.

455
00:29:32,937 --> 00:29:35,940
That's why I'll never trust that woman.

456
00:29:36,191 --> 00:29:39,152
[suspenseful music playing]

457
00:29:41,112 --> 00:29:43,615
[Mercedes] So, what's going
to be our next move?

458
00:29:43,698 --> 00:29:45,033
Who goes first?

459
00:29:45,408 --> 00:29:47,786
Julio or Lily Cruz?

460
00:29:48,203 --> 00:29:52,540
As much as I hate Julio, he has resources,

461
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:57,003
and can still be of use to us.
Pack your bags, Mercedes.

462
00:29:57,629 --> 00:30:00,757
It's time for me
to meet the devil himself.

463
00:30:01,758 --> 00:30:04,552
[suspenseful music playing]

464
00:30:32,872 --> 00:30:35,792
[suspenseful music playing]

465
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:52,100
WELCOME TO POBLACION ARDIENTE

466
00:30:52,183 --> 00:30:58,231
Welcome to Poblacion Ardiente.
My new home.

467
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:02,986
[suspenseful music playing]

468
00:31:09,826 --> 00:31:12,120
[foreboding music playing]

469
00:31:30,513 --> 00:31:31,347
[Jose exhales sharply]

470
00:31:31,431 --> 00:31:32,515
Sir…

471
00:31:34,642 --> 00:31:35,727
You have a visitor.

472
00:31:36,644 --> 00:31:39,188
[gloomy tense music playing]

473
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:51,784
Governor Ruiz!

474
00:31:52,243 --> 00:31:54,579
Here's my proposal for the charity event.

475
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:56,831
I hope it reaches Ms. Montoya.

476
00:31:58,124 --> 00:31:59,167
[Emilia] Hmm…

477
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:03,129
I'm sure you and Helena Montoya
have already met.

478
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,255
[tense music playing]

479
00:32:04,339 --> 00:32:06,799
You know, I wouldn't be surprised because…

480
00:32:07,258 --> 00:32:09,636
you're like a leech.

481
00:32:10,386 --> 00:32:15,725
You really enjoy sucking
other people's wealth.

482
00:32:15,808 --> 00:32:18,144
[chuckles] That poor woman.

483
00:32:18,519 --> 00:32:21,522
All she wanted was to help
but you've got other plans.

484
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:22,774
To exploit her.

485
00:32:23,900 --> 00:32:27,487
I have no interest
in Helena Montoya's wealth

486
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:30,073
because I don't need it.

487
00:32:30,156 --> 00:32:33,076
But you, though? You know, Governor Ruiz,

488
00:32:33,159 --> 00:32:35,662
I'm here because I want to make sure

489
00:32:35,745 --> 00:32:39,123
that Helena Montoya's help
goes to our people,

490
00:32:39,207 --> 00:32:42,126
and not to this joke right in front of me!

491
00:32:43,670 --> 00:32:45,254
The Corruption Queen!

492
00:32:45,338 --> 00:32:47,006
-[tense music playing]
-[laughs]

493
00:32:47,090 --> 00:32:50,218
Yeah, right. I so know you.

494
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:52,720
From the time that you were Ivy Aguas,

495
00:32:52,804 --> 00:32:56,432
and then now, Lily Cruz. [giggles]

496
00:32:56,516 --> 00:32:58,309
I know what you're like.

497
00:32:58,601 --> 00:33:03,731
You're so fond of clinging
to filthy rich people. [laughs]

498
00:33:03,815 --> 00:33:08,444
Well, you know, what can you
expect from someone like you

499
00:33:08,528 --> 00:33:11,447
who's a bloodsucker?

500
00:33:11,531 --> 00:33:12,740
[laughing]

501
00:33:13,366 --> 00:33:17,829
Anyway, good luck. Good luck. Good luck!

502
00:33:17,912 --> 00:33:19,288
Hey! Watch it!

503
00:33:19,372 --> 00:33:20,707
-Sorry, ma'am.
-Get out of my way!

504
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,208
Who told you to stand there?!

505
00:33:22,667 --> 00:33:25,753
-[chuckles]
-[tense music playing]

506
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:33,970
[Emilia] Open the gate!

507
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:45,940
[slow romantic music playing]

508
00:34:22,185 --> 00:34:25,146
[slow romantic music playing]

509
00:34:45,166 --> 00:34:46,292
[suspenseful sting]

510
00:34:49,754 --> 00:34:51,506
Hello, ex-lover.

511
00:34:52,882 --> 00:34:54,050
Helena.

512
00:34:56,511 --> 00:34:57,720
You came back.

513
00:34:59,305 --> 00:35:04,018
Yes, I'm back. Well and alive.

514
00:35:05,311 --> 00:35:09,524
[suspenseful music playing]

515
00:35:18,699 --> 00:35:21,077
[suspenseful music intensifies]

516
00:35:25,915 --> 00:35:28,126
Give us some privacy. Leave us!

517
00:35:29,669 --> 00:35:33,172
[gloomy music playing]

518
00:35:45,101 --> 00:35:46,102
[snaps fingers]

519
00:35:51,065 --> 00:35:52,525
[tense music playing]

520
00:35:52,608 --> 00:35:53,901
How have you been, Julio?

521
00:35:55,069 --> 00:35:56,571
You're looking…

522
00:35:58,781 --> 00:35:59,699
old.

523
00:35:59,782 --> 00:36:00,658
And…

524
00:36:01,701 --> 00:36:02,785
you smell it too.

525
00:36:02,869 --> 00:36:04,245
The stench of death.

526
00:36:05,830 --> 00:36:08,833
[laughing]

527
00:36:12,086 --> 00:36:14,922
-What are you doing here?
-You know why I'm here.

528
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:18,259
You did terrible things to me, Julio.

529
00:36:20,261 --> 00:36:24,891
You killed my father,
you took away my daughter,

530
00:36:24,974 --> 00:36:26,642
and made me believe she was dead.

531
00:36:26,976 --> 00:36:30,646
-Get over it.
-Get over it?! Just like that?!

532
00:36:32,857 --> 00:36:36,861
You can no longer deprive me
of my right to be a mother.

533
00:36:37,945 --> 00:36:40,698
You voided your right
to be a mother when you--

534
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:42,617
Cheated?! [laughs]

535
00:36:43,034 --> 00:36:45,119
I didn't cheat on you, Julio.

536
00:36:46,370 --> 00:36:49,165
You're just not man enough to admit it.

537
00:36:51,417 --> 00:36:53,711
-Don't push my… buttons.
-[suspenseful sting]

538
00:36:55,087 --> 00:36:57,256
[Helena] I'm not the same Helena

539
00:36:57,715 --> 00:37:00,801
you used to belittle and trample on,

540
00:37:00,885 --> 00:37:02,929
just like the other women in your life.

541
00:37:03,012 --> 00:37:05,389
[gloomy tense music playing]

542
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:08,351
Have you heard…

543
00:37:10,519 --> 00:37:13,439
of Red Dragon?

544
00:37:21,322 --> 00:37:23,074
I am Red Dragon.

545
00:37:23,574 --> 00:37:25,117
[suspenseful music playing]

546
00:37:25,201 --> 00:37:32,166
I am powerful, stronger,
a survivor, a fighter.

547
00:37:32,250 --> 00:37:34,669
And no man can put me down.

548
00:37:35,711 --> 00:37:37,922
[suspenseful music playing]

549
00:37:38,673 --> 00:37:41,384
[laughs] Is that fear
I see in your eyes, Julio?

550
00:37:42,927 --> 00:37:44,720
Why don't you just admit it?

551
00:37:46,264 --> 00:37:48,975
You're not in a position to brag.

552
00:37:50,643 --> 00:37:53,396
Everybody in Ardiente hates you.

553
00:37:53,813 --> 00:37:56,732
The people of this town detest you.

554
00:37:57,525 --> 00:37:59,318
Your daughter's rebelling against you.

555
00:37:59,860 --> 00:38:03,781
And your whole house is crumbling down.

556
00:38:04,824 --> 00:38:10,288
The Ardiente family
is slowly breaking apart.

557
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:13,082
But don't worry.

558
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:17,795
There is a new sheriff in town,
and her name is Red Dragon.

559
00:38:22,091 --> 00:38:25,219
[whispering] Until next time, ex-lover.

560
00:38:29,598 --> 00:38:31,475
[tense music playing]

561
00:38:46,532 --> 00:38:53,372
Alpha Mike Foxtrot!
It's all I can say. Darn!

562
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:56,292
[breathing sharply]

563
00:38:56,584 --> 00:38:58,794
[tense music playing]

564
00:39:14,602 --> 00:39:16,645
[dramatic tense music playing]

565
00:39:40,544 --> 00:39:44,215
-[dramatic tense music playing]
-[objects clatter]

566
00:39:55,017 --> 00:39:56,227
[music stops]

567
00:40:02,024 --> 00:40:05,069
Mama? You wanted to talk to me?

568
00:40:05,653 --> 00:40:06,862
Yes, Emilia.

569
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:12,952
The time has come for you
to know the whole truth.

570
00:40:14,870 --> 00:40:17,123
[slow romantic music playing]

571
00:40:18,707 --> 00:40:21,377
[young Julio] <i>Once I achieve</i>
<i>my dream of becoming president,</i>

572
00:40:23,879 --> 00:40:25,423
<i>you'll be my first lady.</i>

573
00:40:26,757 --> 00:40:30,010
<i>Of course, Julio. I love you.</i>

574
00:40:31,137 --> 00:40:32,596
<i>I love you too, Helena.</i>

575
00:40:38,018 --> 00:40:40,729
<i>I'll ask my papa to support</i>
<i>your campaign for councilor.</i>

576
00:40:42,273 --> 00:40:43,983
<i>This is the first step to our dreams.</i>

577
00:40:45,317 --> 00:40:47,069
<i>Will Mr. Ramon say yes?</i>

578
00:40:47,403 --> 00:40:51,407
<i>Julio, I'll do everything</i>
<i>to convince Papa.</i>

579
00:40:52,616 --> 00:40:56,662
<i>I promise you. Our dreams will come true.</i>

580
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:02,543
[Ramon] <i>Helena, I won't support</i>
<i>Julio's campaign.</i>

581
00:41:02,626 --> 00:41:04,545
<i>I trust Ponce more.</i>

582
00:41:05,921 --> 00:41:09,925
<i>But, Papa, Julio promised</i>
<i>to help our business</i>

583
00:41:10,009 --> 00:41:11,510
<i>once he's in power.</i>

584
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:16,015
<i>Look, Helena.</i>
<i>I'm running a delicate business.</i>

585
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:18,601
<i>And you're too young to understand this.</i>

586
00:41:19,018 --> 00:41:24,648
<i>I need to be able to trust</i>
<i>every person in power.</i>

587
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:26,859
<i>If one of them proves to be the weak link</i>

588
00:41:26,942 --> 00:41:28,360
<i>and gets intimidated by the police,</i>

589
00:41:28,944 --> 00:41:30,362
<i>we'll all go down.</i>

590
00:41:30,446 --> 00:41:32,615
<i>Papa, please. Just think it over.</i>

591
00:41:33,115 --> 00:41:34,283
<i>Please.</i>

592
00:41:34,366 --> 00:41:35,743
-[Ramon] <i>Enrique.</i>
-<i>Mr. Ramon.</i>

593
00:41:36,243 --> 00:41:38,704
<i>Thanks for dropping by.</i>
<i>We've got a lot to discuss.</i>

594
00:41:39,079 --> 00:41:40,247
<i>I know.</i>

595
00:41:40,331 --> 00:41:41,999
<i>Rodolfo's in a bind again up north.</i>

596
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:43,918
[scoffs, clicks tongue]

597
00:41:44,251 --> 00:41:45,878
<i>I've been thinking</i>

598
00:41:46,921 --> 00:41:49,131
<i>that you should manage</i>
<i>our shipments there.</i>

599
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,760
<i>Of all my partners, you're the</i>
<i>only one who hasn't failed me.</i>

600
00:41:52,843 --> 00:41:54,970
<i>Go on, Helena. Get some rest.</i>

601
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:57,932
<i>Enrique.</i>

602
00:41:58,015 --> 00:41:59,558
-[Enrique] <i>Sir.</i>
-[Ramon] <i>Follow me.</i>

603
00:42:00,976 --> 00:42:03,729
[Enrique] <i>Thank you</i>
<i>for accepting my invitation.</i>

604
00:42:04,396 --> 00:42:05,898
<i>Although, I think your father</i>
<i>just made you do it.</i>

605
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:07,650
[young Helena] <i>Not really.</i>

606
00:42:08,692 --> 00:42:09,735
[laughs]

607
00:42:09,818 --> 00:42:11,195
<i>I knew it.</i>

608
00:42:12,404 --> 00:42:14,490
<i>Your father wants me for you, doesn't he?</i>

609
00:42:14,990 --> 00:42:16,242
<i>I don't know.</i>

610
00:42:16,659 --> 00:42:18,285
<i>You're the only one who doesn't like me.</i>

611
00:42:18,619 --> 00:42:22,456
<i>Truth is, I can get any woman,</i>
<i>but not you.</i>

612
00:42:22,790 --> 00:42:24,083
<i>I'm sorry, Enrique.</i>

613
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:26,669
<i>But I'm in love with another man.</i>

614
00:42:26,752 --> 00:42:28,796
<i>Julio Ardiente.</i>

615
00:42:31,966 --> 00:42:34,593
<i>He's also the reason I accepted</i>
<i>your invitation, Enrique.</i>

616
00:42:34,885 --> 00:42:37,471
<i>I wanted to discuss</i>
<i>Julio's campaign with you.</i>

617
00:42:38,180 --> 00:42:42,059
<i>I hope you can convince Papa</i>
<i>to side with the Ardientes,</i>

618
00:42:42,142 --> 00:42:43,477
<i>and support him.</i>

619
00:42:44,311 --> 00:42:46,021
<i>Of all Papa's associates,</i>

620
00:42:46,564 --> 00:42:48,232
<i>you're the only one he listens to.</i>

621
00:42:50,317 --> 00:42:55,531
<i>Okay. I'll do it. But on one condition.</i>

622
00:42:55,864 --> 00:42:56,657
<i>What?</i>

623
00:42:56,740 --> 00:42:59,451
[Enrique] <i>You'll give me</i>
<i>a chance to love you.</i>

624
00:43:01,078 --> 00:43:02,162
-[suspenseful sting]
-[camera shutter clicks]

625
00:43:02,246 --> 00:43:03,539
[muffled exclaim]

626
00:43:05,332 --> 00:43:07,001
-<i>What the hell?!</i>
-[chuckles]

627
00:43:07,626 --> 00:43:08,544
<i>Get lost!</i>

628
00:43:10,588 --> 00:43:11,797
[gate squeaks open]

629
00:43:15,551 --> 00:43:17,886
[suspenseful music playing]

630
00:43:24,518 --> 00:43:25,269
<i>Julio.</i>

631
00:43:30,482 --> 00:43:32,276
<i>-Julio, wait.</i>
<i>-You tramp!</i>

632
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:33,944
<i>You cheated on me!</i>

633
00:43:34,028 --> 00:43:36,572
<i>That's not true! It's not!</i>

634
00:43:36,655 --> 00:43:39,366
<i>I just went with Enrique to convince him</i>

635
00:43:39,450 --> 00:43:41,660
<i>to persuade Papa to support you!</i>

636
00:43:41,744 --> 00:43:43,120
<i>Don't try to fool me!</i>

637
00:43:43,203 --> 00:43:46,290
<i>No, Julio! Don't! Please!</i>

638
00:43:46,915 --> 00:43:51,045
<i>I'm pregnant! We're going to have a baby.</i>

639
00:43:51,128 --> 00:43:53,547
<i>That's why I'm helping you</i>
<i>reach your dreams.</i>

640
00:43:53,631 --> 00:43:55,799
<i>We're going to have a family!</i>

641
00:43:56,091 --> 00:43:57,968
<i>And yet, you're being a flirt!</i>

642
00:43:58,677 --> 00:43:59,803
<i>No.</i>

643
00:44:00,387 --> 00:44:02,097
<i>You have no right to that child!</i>

644
00:44:02,431 --> 00:44:05,184
<i>You have no right to be a mother</i>
<i>or to be my wife!</i>

645
00:44:06,268 --> 00:44:07,311
[sobbing]

646
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:14,485
<i>Julio, wait! Julio! Julio! Please! Julio!</i>

647
00:44:15,736 --> 00:44:18,030
-[screaming in pain]
-[doctor] <i>Push. Push. Push.</i>

648
00:44:18,322 --> 00:44:20,908
<i>Push. Push. Almost there.</i>

649
00:44:20,991 --> 00:44:22,993
-[grunting, screaming in pain]
-[doctor] <i>Almost there.</i>

650
00:44:23,077 --> 00:44:25,162
<i>The head's coming out.</i>

651
00:44:26,872 --> 00:44:28,290
[suspenseful music playing]

652
00:44:28,374 --> 00:44:29,416
[tires screech]

653
00:44:39,426 --> 00:44:40,469
<i>Ramon.</i>

654
00:44:41,178 --> 00:44:42,137
<i>Julio.</i>

655
00:44:42,388 --> 00:44:44,890
<i>What are you doing here? What's going on?</i>

656
00:44:46,350 --> 00:44:47,309
[gunshot]

657
00:44:49,186 --> 00:44:50,145
-[gunshot]
-[grunts]

658
00:44:53,565 --> 00:44:56,235
-<i>Doc, how's my baby?</i>
-[baby crying]

659
00:44:57,903 --> 00:45:01,365
<i>Doc? What are you doing?</i>

660
00:45:03,742 --> 00:45:05,828
<i>Doc, where are you taking my baby?</i>

661
00:45:06,245 --> 00:45:07,496
[doctor] <i>There's been a problem.</i>

662
00:45:07,579 --> 00:45:09,248
<i>-But I promise, we will do everything…</i>
<i>-Doc, my baby!</i>

663
00:45:09,331 --> 00:45:10,541
<i>-…to save your baby.</i>
<i>-Wait, that's my baby!</i>

664
00:45:10,624 --> 00:45:12,751
<i>She's taking my baby!</i>
<i>Didn't you hear her?!</i>

665
00:45:13,043 --> 00:45:16,964
<i>My baby! Doc! Doc!</i>

666
00:45:17,047 --> 00:45:19,341
<i>Mr. Julio, here's your baby.</i>

667
00:45:20,509 --> 00:45:23,345
[dark tense music playing]

668
00:45:29,977 --> 00:45:33,730
<i>Emilia. I'll name you Emilia.</i>

669
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,817
[dark tense music playing]

670
00:45:48,871 --> 00:45:49,913
[young Helena] <i>Doc.</i>

671
00:45:51,874 --> 00:45:53,333
<i>I'm sorry, Helena.</i>

672
00:45:53,959 --> 00:45:55,919
<i>Your baby developed some complications.</i>

673
00:45:57,296 --> 00:45:59,631
<i>-Huh?</i>
<i>-She didn't make it.</i>

674
00:46:00,507 --> 00:46:02,718
[sobbing]

675
00:46:02,801 --> 00:46:04,803
[young Helena] <i>That can't be true, Doc!</i>

676
00:46:04,887 --> 00:46:06,597
-[doctor] <i>I'm sorry.</i>
-[young Helena] <i>How?!</i>

677
00:46:08,390 --> 00:46:11,810
<i>She was crying</i>
<i>when I gave birth to her, Doc!</i>

678
00:46:13,270 --> 00:46:17,149
-[dramatic music playing]
-[sobbing]

679
00:46:27,201 --> 00:46:29,161
[suspenseful music playing]

680
00:46:30,871 --> 00:46:32,247
[young Helena] <i>I promise</i>

681
00:46:33,081 --> 00:46:35,417
<i>to continue what you started, Papa.</i>

682
00:46:36,376 --> 00:46:38,795
<i>I'll make your business grow,</i>

683
00:46:38,879 --> 00:46:41,798
<i>and I will make it</i>
<i>the biggest in the country.</i>

684
00:46:43,425 --> 00:46:45,969
<i>No one will dare to compete with us.</i>

685
00:46:47,387 --> 00:46:48,722
<i>I swear</i>

686
00:46:49,598 --> 00:46:53,936
<i>that one day, I'll avenge your death.</i>

687
00:47:01,151 --> 00:47:04,279
<i>Ms. Helena, the guns</i>
<i>from China have arrived.</i>

688
00:47:06,156 --> 00:47:07,157
<i>Let's go.</i>

689
00:47:07,241 --> 00:47:10,077
[gloomy music playing]

690
00:47:14,706 --> 00:47:16,542
Now, do you see how evil your father is?

691
00:47:18,001 --> 00:47:19,127
Mama.

692
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,965
[sobbing]

693
00:47:25,884 --> 00:47:29,096
He killed my father and separated us.

694
00:47:32,683 --> 00:47:34,893
The time has come for my revenge.

695
00:47:35,477 --> 00:47:38,230
[suspenseful music playing]

696
00:47:50,742 --> 00:47:54,246
[Julio] <i>I've erased you from my life once.</i>

697
00:47:55,622 --> 00:47:57,916
<i>And I can do it again, Helena.</i>

698
00:47:59,251 --> 00:48:06,049
<i>Those who play with fire,</i>
<i>with Julio Ardiente, will burn!</i>

699
00:48:07,759 --> 00:48:12,639
[sinister music swelling]

700
00:48:17,519 --> 00:48:18,979
[Camia] <i>Lily, are you sure we're going</i>

701
00:48:19,062 --> 00:48:21,481
<i>to that Helena Montoya's charity event?</i>

702
00:48:21,565 --> 00:48:22,733
[Lily] <i>That's where I'll find out</i>

703
00:48:22,816 --> 00:48:24,776
<i>whether she's my enemy or my ally.</i>

704
00:48:24,860 --> 00:48:27,863
<i>I'm going to donate</i>
<i>20 million worth of diamonds</i>

705
00:48:27,946 --> 00:48:29,865
<i>to the people of Ardiente.</i>

706
00:48:29,948 --> 00:48:32,034
[Raul] <i>It won't reach the charity event</i>

707
00:48:32,117 --> 00:48:33,410
<i>because we'll take all of it.</i>

708
00:48:33,493 --> 00:48:35,329
<i>Only an idiot would betray Red Dragon.</i>

709
00:48:35,412 --> 00:48:36,580
[henchman] <i>Someone's following us.</i>

710
00:48:36,663 --> 00:48:37,539
[gunfire]

711
00:48:37,623 --> 00:48:39,541
<i>I would like to introduce to you</i>

712
00:48:39,625 --> 00:48:44,212
<i>my long-lost daughter,</i>
<i>Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

713
00:48:44,296 --> 00:48:46,965
[applause]

714
00:48:47,049 --> 00:48:50,719
[theme music playing]
